<helpdocument version="1.0">
<meta>
<topic id="textscalc01func_iferrorxml" indexer="include" status="PUBLISH">
<title id="tit" xml-lang="en-US">IFERROR</title>
<filename>/text/scalc/01/func_iferror.xhp</filename>
</topic>
</meta>
<body>
<bookmark xml-lang="en-US" branch="index" id="bm_id3170001">
<bookmark_value>IFERROR function</bookmark_value>
<bookmark_value>error handling;IFERROR</bookmark_value>
</bookmark>
<bookmark xml-lang="en-US" branch="hid/SC_HID_FUNC_IFERROR" id="bm_id3170002" localize="false"/>
<paragraph role="heading" id="hd_id3170001" xml-lang="en-US" level="2" l10n="NEW"><variable id="iferror"><link href="text/scalc/01/func_iferror.xhp">IFERROR</link>
</variable></paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3170003" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="NEW"><ahelp hid="HID_FUNC_IFERROR">Returns the value if it is not an error value, otherwise it returns the alternative value.</ahelp> Every error value is replaced, including #N/A; ordinary values pass through unchanged.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="heading" id="hd_id3170004" xml-lang="en-US" level="3" l10n="NEW">Syntax</paragraph>
<paragraph role="code" id="par_id3170005" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="NEW">IFERROR(Value; Alternative)</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3170006" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="NEW"><emph>Value</emph> is the value or reference to be checked for an error value.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3170007" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="NEW"><emph>Alternative</emph> is the value returned when <emph>Value</emph> is an error value. It is evaluated only when <emph>Value</emph> is an error value; an error in <emph>Alternative</emph> itself is returned.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="heading" id="hd_id3170008" xml-lang="en-US" level="3" l10n="NEW">Remarks</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3170009" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="NEW">A reference to an empty cell is not an error value, so <emph>Value</emph> is returned and shows as 0.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3170010" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="NEW">In an array formula, each element of <emph>Value</emph> that is an error value is replaced on its own; if <emph>Alternative</emph> is also a range or array, the matching element of <emph>Alternative</emph> is used.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3170011" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="NEW">To replace only #N/A and keep other error values, use IFNA.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="heading" id="hd_id3170012" xml-lang="en-US" level="3" l10n="NEW">Example</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3170013" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="NEW"><item type="input">=IFERROR(1/0; "fallback")</item> returns <quote>fallback</quote>.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3170014" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="NEW"><item type="input">=IFERROR(SQRT(-1); 10)</item> returns 10, because the square root of a negative number gives the error Err:502.</paragraph>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3170015" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="NEW"><item type="input">=IFERROR(5; 1/0)</item> returns 5; the alternative is not evaluated.</paragraph>
<embed href="text/shared/00/00000001.xhp#siehe"/>
<paragraph role="paragraph" id="par_id3170016" xml-lang="en-US" l10n="NEW"><link href="text/scalc/01/func_ifna.xhp" name="IFNA">IFNA</link>, <link href="text/scalc/01/04060104.xhp#iserror" name="ISERROR">ISERROR</link>.</paragraph>
</body>
</helpdocument>
